WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.960
Delhi, the Red Fort, November

2
00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:04.840
nineteen forty five.

3
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:07.040
Three officers on trial, and a

4
00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.590
whole country listening.

5
00:00:09.179 --> 00:00:11.059
All three had served in the

6
00:00:11.059 --> 00:00:13.659
Indian National Army, led by

7
00:00:13.659 --> 00:00:16.369
Subhas Bose in South East Asia.

8
00:00:16.907 --> 00:00:18.207
The charge:

9
00:00:18.207 --> 00:00:20.607
waging war against the King.

10
00:00:20.607 --> 00:00:23.107
Shah Nawaz Khan, Sahgal and

11
00:00:23.107 --> 00:00:26.567
Dhillon. One Muslim, one Hindu,

12
00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:27.657
one Sikh.

13
00:00:28.124 --> 00:00:30.244
The trial became, in one

14
00:00:30.244 --> 00:00:32.464
biographer's words, a dramatic

15
00:00:32.464 --> 00:00:34.624
symbol of national unity.

16
00:00:34.624 --> 00:00:36.364
The Congress and the Muslim

17
00:00:36.364 --> 00:00:38.634
League both took up their cause.

18
00:00:39.226 --> 00:00:41.446
Seventeen lawyers came to defend

19
00:00:41.446 --> 00:00:44.466
them. One was Jawaharlal Nehru,

20
00:00:44.466 --> 00:00:46.606
in a barrister's gown he had not

21
00:00:46.606 --> 00:00:48.516
worn for thirty years.

22
00:00:49.068 --> 00:00:51.288
The lead counsel, Bhulabhai

23
00:00:51.288 --> 00:00:54.268
Desai, already unwell, argued

24
00:00:54.268 --> 00:00:55.848
they had fought as an organised

25
00:00:55.848 --> 00:00:57.898
army, for freedom.

26
00:00:58.486 --> 00:01:01.446
Judge them, he said, no more and

27
00:01:01.446 --> 00:01:03.696
no less than your own men.

28
00:01:04.486 --> 00:01:06.146
The court found them guilty.

29
00:01:06.146 --> 00:01:08.716
Transportation for life.

30
00:01:09.486 --> 00:01:11.106
But the Commander in Chief,

31
00:01:11.106 --> 00:01:13.386
Auchinleck, read the mood of the

32
00:01:13.386 --> 00:01:15.246
country, and of the army.

33
00:01:15.246 --> 00:01:17.206
He remitted the sentences.

34
00:01:17.206 --> 00:01:19.626
The government had won the case,

35
00:01:19.626 --> 00:01:21.596
and lost the argument.

36
00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:23.507
For GS1:

37
00:01:23.507 --> 00:01:25.640
the INA trials, Red Fort,

38
00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:26.827
nineteen forty five.

39
00:01:26.827 --> 00:01:29.560
A defence led by Bhulabhai

40
00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:32.680
Desai, a country united, and an

41
00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:34.220
army whose loyalty to the Raj

42
00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:35.250
